      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Show People** kicked off a rich tradition of Hollywood examining itself on screen. Its DNA can be found in **Mulholland Drive** (2001), **The Player** (1992), and **Once Upon a Time in Hollywood** (2019). The film's brilliant balance of insider satire and genuine affection for the movie industry created a template that filmmakers still follow nearly a century later."
